{"id":"10-course-correcting","number":10,"slug":"when-agents-go-wrong","title":"When the agent goes off the rails","short":"When agents go off the rails","module":"Working with one agent","summary":"Every agent goes off the rails sometimes. The skill isn't avoiding it; it's noticing early and recovering cheaply. Learn the warning signs, the recovery ladder from a quick interrupt to throwing the work away, and the habits that make recovery cheap.","voice":"Eric","scenes":[{"template":"title","chapter":"Intro","narration":"Every agent goes off the rails sometimes. The skill isn't avoiding it. It's noticing early, and recovering cheaply.","params":{"kicker":"Lesson 10","module":"Module 2 · Working with one agent","title":"When the agent goes *off the rails*","subtitle":"Warning signs, the recovery ladder, and cheap do-overs.","bubble":"Oops. Rewind?","mood":"alert"},"start":0.5,"dur":8.671,"words":[{"text":"Every","s":0.8,"e":1.12},{"text":"agent","s":1.2,"e":1.52},{"text":"goes","s":1.56,"e":1.68},{"text":"off","s":1.76,"e":1.92},{"text":"the","s":1.96,"e":2},{"text":"rails","s":2.16,"e":2.32},{"text":"sometimes.","s":2.68,"e":3.44},{"text":"The","s":3.48,"e":3.52},{"text":"skill","s":3.6,"e":3.92},{"text":"isn't","s":4,"e":4.24},{"text":"avoiding","s":4.44,"e":4.72},{"text":"it.","s":4.8,"e":5.36},{"text":"It's","s":5.44,"e":5.6},{"text":"noticing","s":5.68,"e":6.16},{"text":"early,","s":6.48,"e":6.853},{"text":"and","s":6.907,"e":6.96},{"text":"recovering","s":7.16,"e":7.6},{"text":"cheaply.","s":7.72,"e":8.32}]},{"template":"statement","chapter":"It's normal","narration":"Ben Vinegar makes a provocative point. If your agent never seems subtly wrong, if you never have to stop and scrutinize, that's a bad sign. It probably means you're just pressing go and merging.","params":{"text":"Never catching your agent being subtly wrong is a *bad sign*.","sub":"It probably means you're just pressing go. — Ben Vinegar","art":"eye","tone":"human","sync":false},"start":9.171,"du